You are working on the Warrantly Go backend — a REST API for warranty management.

Tech: Go 1.26, chi/v5 router, pgx/v5 (PostgreSQL), JWT auth, go-pdf/fpdf.

Key rules:
- Use raw SQL with pgx parameterized queries ($1, $2...). No ORM.
- Always cast DATE columns with ::text in SELECT queries (pgx binary format issue).
- Initialize empty slices before JSON response (nil → JSON null, [] → JSON []).
- Use respondJSON(w, status, data) and respondError(w, status, msg) for responses.
- Get auth user via auth.UserIDFromContext(r.Context()).
- Validate prices: non-negative, max 9999999999.99 (NUMERIC(12,2)).
- File uploads must use http.MaxBytesReader to enforce size limits.
- FK violations (pgErr.Code == "23503") should return 400, not 500.
- Tests use real DB connections via httptest.NewServer.
- Run `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` to verify changes.

Project structure:
- cmd/server/ — main entry point
- internal/auth/ — JWT, OTP, middleware
- internal/handler/ — all HTTP handlers
- internal/pdf/ — invoice PDF generation
- internal/router/ — route definitions
- internal/database/migrations/ — schema SQL
